# AI Task Orchestrator - Complete Lifecycle Flow

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant App as Orchestrator User
  participant Orc as AITaskOrchestrator
  participant Obs as Observability (Metrics/Tracer)
  participant PM as PluginManager
  participant Mem as Memory/Store

  App->>Orc: instantiate()
  rect rgb(240,245,255)
    note right of Orc: Lazy init (if available)
    Orc-->>Obs: get_metrics_collector? / get_tracer?
    Orc-->>PM: get_plugin_manager?
  end

  App->>+Orc: __enter__/__aenter__()
  alt plugins available
    Orc->>PM: startup()
  else plugins unavailable
    note over Orc: skip plugin hooks
  end
  Orc->>Mem: load context/memory

  App->>+Orc: execute_task_step(...)
  Orc->>Obs: record metrics/trace (guarded)
  Orc->>Mem: read/write insights (robust shape handling)
  Orc-->>App: result or raise ExecutionError (chained)

  App->>+Orc: __exit__/__aexit__(exc?)
  alt plugins available
    Orc->>PM: shutdown()
  else
    note over Orc: no-op
  end
  Orc-->>App: closed (bool in async)
```

## Description

This comprehensive diagram shows the complete lifecycle of the AI Task Orchestrator:

1. **Instantiation**: Lazy initialization of observability and plugin components
2. **Context entry**: Startup hooks and memory loading when entering context
3. **Task execution**: Metrics recording, memory operations, and error handling
4. **Context exit**: Graceful shutdown with plugin cleanup
5. **Error handling**: Robust error chaining and exception management throughout

## Sequence Point Index

1. **Orchestrator instantiation** - App creates new AITaskOrchestrator instance
2. **Observability component check** - Orchestrator attempts to get metrics collector (if available)
3. **Tracer component check** - Orchestrator attempts to get tracer (if available)
4. **Plugin manager check** - Orchestrator attempts to get plugin manager (if available)
5. **Context manager entry** - App enters orchestrator context via `__enter__()` or `__aenter__()`
6. **Plugin startup** - If plugins available, orchestrator calls PluginManager startup()
7. **Memory context loading** - Orchestrator loads context/memory from Memory/Store
8. **Task step execution** - App calls `execute_task_step()` with task parameters
9. **Metrics recording** - Orchestrator records metrics/trace (with guard checks)
10. **Memory operations** - Orchestrator performs read/write insights with robust shape handling
11. **Result or error return** - Orchestrator returns result or raises ExecutionError with chaining
12. **Context manager exit** - App exits context via `__exit__()` or `__aexit__()`
13. **Plugin shutdown** - If plugins available, orchestrator calls PluginManager shutdown()
14. **Context closure confirmation** - Orchestrator confirms closed state (returns bool in async)
